          "source": "lem-cg-weak-parabolic-projection-and-cover-joins",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "**(1) Inversion set of the prefix.** For every $w\\in W$,\n\n$$N(w_J^{-1})=N(w^{-1})\\cap\\Phi_{J,+}.$$\n\nConsequently $w_J$ is the greatest element of $W_J$ below $w$ in $\\le_R$, the map $w\\mapsto w_J$ is order-preserving, and for every $v\\in W_J$ one has $v\\le_R w$ if and only if $v\\le_R w_J$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "1.2",
            "3.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "thm-cg-finite-parabolic-longest-element-and-opposition",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "(ii) $\\ell(w_0)=|N(w_0)|=|\\Phi_+|=|T|$, and $\\rho(w_0)\\Phi_+=\\Phi_-$;\n\n(iii) $\\ell(w_0w)=\\ell(w_0)-\\ell(w)$ and $\\ell(ww_0)=\\ell(w_0)-\\ell(w)$ for every $w\\in W$; consequently $\\ell(w_0)=\\max\\{\\ell(w):w\\in W\\}$ and $w_0$ is the unique element of that length (the element of longest length);\n\n(iv) $w_0^2=1$;\n\n(v) $w_0Sw_0^{-1}=S$, and there is a permutation $\\sigma$ of $S$ with $\\rho(w_0)e_s=-e_{\\sigma(s)}$, equivalently $w_0sw_0=\\sigma(s)$, for every $s\\in S$.",
