          "quote": "The $c^\\infty$**-sorting word** of $w$ is the lexicographically earliest admissible position set for $w$: least first position, then least second position, and so on. The **block sequence** of an admissible position set is the sequence $T_1,T_2,\\dots$ in which $T_j\\subseteq S$ is the set of letters of the subword occurring between the $(j-1)$-st and the $j$-th divider; it is read up to the last nonempty set.",
          "uses": [
