    "ex-cg-cambrian-quotient-of-s3-and-two-orientations": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "def-cg-coxeter-oriented-euler-form-and-c-sorting-word",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The $c^\\infty$**-sorting word** of $w$ is the lexicographically earliest admissible position set for $w$: least first position, then least second position, and so on. The **block sequence** of an admissible position set is the sequence $T_1,T_2,\\dots$ in which $T_j\\subseteq S$ is the set of letters of the subword occurring between the $(j-1)$-st and the $j$-th divider; it is read up to the last nonempty set.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "1.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "def-cg-sortable-element-skip-roots-and-cone",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "An element $v\\in W$ is $c$**-sortable** when the block sequence $(T_1,T_2,\\dots)$ of its $c^\\infty$-sorting word is weakly decreasing under inclusion: $T_1\\supseteq T_2\\supseteq\\cdots$.",
          "uses": [
            "1.2",
            "1.3",
            "5.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F3",
          "source": "def-cg-initial-letter-sortable-projection",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "\\pi_c(w):=\\begin{cases}1&\\text{if }w=1,\\\\ s\\cdot\\pi_{scs}(sw)&\\text{if }\\ell(sw)<\\ell(w),\\\\ \\pi_{sc}(w_J)&\\text{if }\\ell(sw)>\\ell(w),\\end{cases}",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F4",
          "source": "def-cg-left-right-weak-order-and-descents",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "$$u\\le_R v\\iff v=ux\\text{ for some }x\\in W\\text{ with }\\ell(v)=\\ell(u)+\\ell(x),$$",
          "uses": [
            "2.2",
            "3.2",
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F5",
          "source": "def-cg-left-right-weak-order-and-descents",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "it is a **right join** (least upper bound) if it is a right upper bound and\n$z\\le_R y$ for every right upper bound $y$ of $A$. Dually, $z$ is a **right\nlower bound** if $z\\le_R a$ for every $a\\in A$, and a **right meet** (greatest\nlower bound) if it is a right lower bound and $u\\le_R z$ for every right lower\nbound $u$ of $A$.",
          "uses": [
            "2.2",
            "3.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F6",
          "source": "thm-cg-weak-order-meet-semilattice-and-finite-lattice",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "If $W$ is finite, then $(W,\\le_R)$ and $(W,\\le_L)$ are lattices with minimum $1$ and maximum $w_0$;",
          "uses": [
            "2.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F7",
          "source": "thm-cg-sortable-projection-greatest-element-and-interval-fibers",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "$$u_c\\colon W\\to W,\\qquad u_c(w):=\\pi_{c^{-1}}(ww_0)\\,w_0,$$",
          "uses": [
            "3.3"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F8",
          "source": "thm-cg-sortable-projection-greatest-element-and-interval-fibers",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "$$\\pi_c(x)=\\pi_c(y)\\iff u_c(x)=u_c(y),\\qquad \\pi_c(u_c(w))=\\pi_c(w),\\qquad u_c(\\pi_c(w))=u_c(w).$$\nConsequently every $\\sim_c$-fiber is the closed interval\n$$[w]_c=\\{y\\in W:\\pi_c(w)\\le_Ry\\le_Ru_c(w)\\}$$\nwith lower endpoint $\\pi_c(w)$ and upper endpoint $u_c(w)$: no fiber has a gap, both endpoint maps are order preserving,",
          "uses": [
            "4.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F9",
          "source": "thm-cg-sortable-meet-join-closure-and-cambrian-quotient",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "For all $x,y\\in W$,\n\n$$\\pi_c(x\\wedge y)=\\pi_c(x)\\wedge\\pi_c(y),\\qquad \\pi_c(x\\vee y)=\\pi_c(x)\\vee\\pi_c(y).$$",
          "uses": [
            "3.2"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F10",
          "source": "def-cg-recursive-sortable-projection-and-cambrian-congruence",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "**(1) Sortable equivalence and quotient order.** Define the **sortable equivalence** $\\sim_c$ on $W$ by\n\n$$x\\sim_c y:\\iff \\pi_c(x)=\\pi_c(y),$$\n\nwrite $[x]_c:=\\{y\\in W:\\pi_c(y)=\\pi_c(x)\\}$ for the $\\sim_c$-class of $x$ and $W/{\\sim_c}:=\\{[x]_c:x\\in W\\}$, and let $p_c\\colon W\\to W/{\\sim_c}$, $p_c(x):=[x]_c$, be the quotient map. The **sortable quotient order** on $W/{\\sim_c}$ is\n\n$$[x]_c\\le_c[y]_c:\\iff \\pi_c(x)\\le_R\\pi_c(y).$$\n\nThis is independent of the chosen representatives because each class has a single $\\pi_c$-image; it is the order induced by $\\le_R$ on the image of $\\pi_c$.",
          "uses": [
            "3.1",
            "3.2"
          ]
        }
      ],
